research/audit/wave6-alpha.md:117:- **Current mathematical surface read:** the four rejected item texts and each cited dependency implicated by the rejection were read from current disk, including the natural-order/induction chain, the extended-real/divergence definitions, and the convex-homotopy dependencies. The inherited open A8 action is to give each of the four current-context Terra rejections a fatal-only owner disposition, append one per-model/per-context ledger row with the present full normalized item hash, repair only any `confirmed_fatal` item, independently certify any Alpha-authored final text, and rejudge exactly the plain list of item ids whose own text changed.
research/audit/wave6-alpha.md:135:- All 13 current frozen-context hashes and judge-normalized item hashes were recomputed through direct `tools/judge.mts --context-hash` calls. Every value exactly matches both corresponding rows in the targeted A7 ledger. The direct coverage pass without nested current-context spawning therefore reports **13/13 paired targets**, with only the four expected adjudicated-nonfatal warnings.
research/audit/wave6-alpha.md:177:- `level-coverage.mjs --verify-current-context` cannot reproduce its aggregate exit in this sandbox because its internal Node `spawnSync` is denied with `EPERM`; the gate presently treats the resulting empty stdout as “not JSON.” This is an execution boundary, not a context mismatch. Direct `judge.mts --context-hash` calls succeed for all 13 targets, and an exhaustive comparison finds **26/26 exact current ledger rows**: one DeepSeek V4 Pro row and one GPT 5.6 Terra row for every current context and judge-normalized item hash. The run state's subprocess-capable authoritative A8 coverage gate remains exit zero.
research/audit/wave6-alpha.md:185:- **Current judge scope and hashes bound to disk:** the current repair receipt names 30 items. The additional A7 calls added 34 rows for 17 newly included items; all transports completed. Six exact-current rejections in that newly swept surface have no owner decision yet: `def-the-diagonal-of-a-space` (`3e4f7f8b63ab058d268723fe7271a80825de167a3e64a47db6999b8e41f0aad7`), `thm-hausdorff-iff-the-diagonal-is-closed` (`8fea93f9d9d8f98b84203acb65796250a536a6c6908d2766f215d79fe0b87a86`), `rem-what-the-diagonal-criterion-gives-and-what-it-costs` (`bfebc1a4aacd425eabdcf839d4928ec7829bcc4751fbd42a39dace093cb32384`), `ex-the-graph-of-a-continuous-real-function-is-closed` (`4fe01c8d4499bdbf3f77f1967fceab9b39cda58c39106e9502d8443d6e544269`), `ex-a-finite-hausdorff-space-is-discrete` (`e38f4906c8772f1d5b3b2785e2ad8d2a91bb127977c73f611391282936eb72d5`), and `lem-a-locally-compact-hausdorff-space-has-a-base-of-open-sets-with-compact-closure` (`d28d42e619a13f35391c8190033ee0456eaa4295d231f95321394f60dd6c5616`). These are full verification-stripped SHA-256 values from `tools/item-hash.mjs`; their current judge contexts and judge-normalized item hashes exactly match the six rejection rows.
